From f4af7d1ca0311dd95982acd73c3f6a859f9a1a71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 342/488] soh: name the 10 address-named symbols defined in
 z_camera.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 10 are defined in soh/src/code/z_camera.c; updating their references touches 10 files in total.

  * func_80043ABC -> Camera_SetDefaultUpdateRates
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loads the camera's yaw, pitch, radius, offset
    and fov update rates from their default REG values.

  * func_80043B60 -> Camera_SetSnapUpdateRates
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sets every update rate to the same REG value
    and the three offset rates to 0.001, so the camera snaps rather than
    easing.

  * func_80044340 -> Camera_BGCheckPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the thin wrapper: runs the same background
    check between two points and writes the corrected position back into the
    second.

  * func_80045508 -> Camera_CheckEyeAtCorner
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the background check both ways between
    the at and eye points and classifies the result, reporting whether the
    two surfaces meet at a corner the swing logic has to peek around.

  * func_800458D4 -> Camera_CalcAtForNormal
    deduced, confidence GUESS: computes the at point for the normal camera
    settings, offsetting it by the player's height, adjusting for the floor
    slope and easing it toward the player as they climb or fall. Named for
    the family of Camera_CalcAt* helpers around it; the file does not name
    it.

  * func_80045B08 -> Camera_CalcAtForTurn
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the same at-point calculation with the offset
    swung to the player's side according to the caller's angle, used while
    the camera turns around them. Named to pair with Camera_CalcAtForNormal.

  * func_80046E20 -> Camera_SwingAroundCollision
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the swing update: it runs the corner check
    and, depending on the result, peeks the eye around the corner, pulls it
    in to the minimum distance or lets it settle back out.

  * func_80057FC4 -> Camera_SetSettingForRoom
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the camera setting from the room's
    behaviour type, forcing CAM_SET_FREE0 for sub-cameras.

  * func_8005B198 -> Camera_GetTargetCategory
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns the actor category the camera last
    locked onto; Bg_Bdan_Switch compares it against its own category to tell
    whether the camera is watching it.

  * func_80043F94 -> Camera_BGCheckLine
    deduced, confidence GUESS: line-tests from a point toward a CamColChk
    target, extending the ray slightly, and fills the check's surface
    normal, polygon and bg id -- the normal is faked from the ray direction
    when nothing is hit. Named BGCheckLine rather than BGCheckInfo because
    the latter already exists in this file as its caller.

